<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Adolphus Frederick III, Duke of Mecklenburg-Strelitz</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1686">1686</a>–<a href="/years/1752">1752</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Adolf Frederick III of Mecklenburg-Strelitz</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Adolphus Frederick III (1686–1752) was Duke of Mecklenburg-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/strelitz">Strelitz</a> from 1708, the second ruler of the duchy created by the partition of Mecklenburg in 1701. After the old residence at Strelitz burned down in 1712, he founded the planned town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neustrelitz">Neustrelitz</a> in 1733 around a new palace, with streets radiating from a central square.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/adolphus-frederick-iii-duke-of-mecklenburg-strelitz.jpg" alt="Adolphus Frederick III, Duke of Mecklenburg-Strelitz" width="320" height="446" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unidentified painter · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Adolf_Friedrich_III,_Duke_of_Mecklenburg-Strelitz.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
